[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: MIL-STD-498 SDD (Software Design Description) - Military Quad Copter RTOS
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1. Scope
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1.1 Identification
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-001-MILUAV
TITLE: Design Identification
STATEMENT: This document shall describe the software design for the Military Quad Copter RTOS, including architecture, components, interfaces, and design decisions for autonomous military UAV operations.
RATIONALE: Clear design identification ensures proper system development and maintenance.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 1.2 System overview
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-002-MILUAV
TITLE: Design Overview
STATEMENT: The Military Quad Copter RTOS shall implement a modular, fault-tolerant architecture with real-time performance, secure communication, and autonomous operation capabilities for military UAV applications.
RATIONALE: Design overview establishes the architectural foundation for system development.
[[/SECTION]]
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 2. Referenced documents
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-003-MILUAV
TITLE: Design Standards
STATEMENT: The software design shall comply with MIL-STD-498, DO-178C Level A, MISRA C/C++, and military software architecture standards for safety-critical systems.
RATIONALE: Design standards ensure software quality, safety, and maintainability.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3. CSCI-wide design decisions
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-004-MILUAV
TITLE: Architecture Decision
STATEMENT: The system shall implement a layered architecture with separation of concerns, including hardware abstraction layer, real-time kernel, middleware services, and application layer with clear interface boundaries.
RATIONALE: Layered architecture enables modular development, testing, and maintenance.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-005-MILUAV
TITLE: Real-Time Design
STATEMENT: The system shall implement priority-based preemptive scheduling with deterministic timing guarantees, interrupt handling, and real-time task management for critical flight control operations.
RATIONALE: Real-time design ensures predictable system behavior and safety.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-006-MILUAV
TITLE: Fault Tolerance Design
STATEMENT: The system shall implement triple-redundant critical components with voting mechanisms, automatic fault detection, isolation, and recovery procedures for high reliability operation.
RATIONALE: Fault tolerance design ensures system reliability under adverse conditions.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4. CSCI architectural design
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4.1 Architecture Overview
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-007-MILUAV
TITLE: System Architecture
STATEMENT: The system shall implement a distributed architecture with flight control computer, mission computer, communication computer, and sensor computer interconnected via high-speed data buses with redundant communication paths.
RATIONALE: Distributed architecture provides fault isolation and system scalability.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-008-MILUAV
TITLE: Component Architecture
STATEMENT: The system shall be organized into flight control, mission management, sensor fusion, communication, security, and power management components with well-defined interfaces and data flow.
RATIONALE: Component architecture enables modular development and system integration.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4.2 Flight Control Component
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-009-MILUAV
TITLE: Flight Control Design
STATEMENT: The flight control component shall implement PID-based control algorithms for attitude, altitude, and position control with adaptive gain scheduling and wind compensation for military operations.
RATIONALE: Flight control design ensures stable and precise UAV operation.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-010-MILUAV
TITLE: Stabilization System
STATEMENT: The stabilization system shall implement quaternion-based attitude estimation, Kalman filtering for sensor fusion, and adaptive control algorithms for robust flight performance.
RATIONALE: Stabilization system provides accurate attitude control and sensor fusion.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-011-MILUAV
TITLE: Navigation System
STATEMENT: The navigation system shall implement waypoint navigation, path planning, obstacle avoidance, and formation flying algorithms with real-time trajectory optimization.
RATIONALE: Navigation system enables autonomous mission execution and collision avoidance.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4.3 Mission Management Component
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-012-MILUAV
TITLE: Mission Planning
STATEMENT: The mission planning component shall implement 3D route optimization, fuel management, payload configuration, and contingency planning with automatic mission adaptation capabilities.
RATIONALE: Mission planning ensures efficient resource utilization and mission success.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-013-MILUAV
TITLE: Mission Execution
STATEMENT: The mission execution component shall implement real-time mission monitoring, automatic decision-making, payload deployment, and mission abort procedures with safety interlocks.
RATIONALE: Mission execution enables autonomous operation with human oversight.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-014-MILUAV
TITLE: Payload Management
STATEMENT: The payload management component shall implement payload configuration, deployment control, data collection, and equipment health monitoring with automatic fault detection.
RATIONALE: Payload management enables diverse mission capabilities and equipment utilization.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4.4 Sensor Fusion Component
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-015-MILUAV
TITLE: Multi-Sensor Fusion
STATEMENT: The sensor fusion component shall implement Kalman filtering, particle filtering, and machine learning algorithms for combining data from GPS, INS, LIDAR, cameras, and environmental sensors.
RATIONALE: Multi-sensor fusion provides robust navigation and environmental awareness.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-016-MILUAV
TITLE: Obstacle Detection
STATEMENT: The obstacle detection component shall implement LIDAR point cloud processing, stereo vision algorithms, and radar signal processing for real-time obstacle detection and avoidance.
RATIONALE: Obstacle detection ensures safe autonomous operation in complex environments.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-017-MILUAV
TITLE: GPS-Denied Navigation
STATEMENT: The GPS-denied navigation component shall implement visual odometry, inertial navigation, and landmark recognition algorithms for operation in GPS-compromised environments.
RATIONALE: GPS-denied navigation enables operations in challenging military environments.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4.5 Communication Component
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-018-MILUAV
TITLE: Secure Communication
STATEMENT: The communication component shall implement AES-256 encryption, frequency hopping, spread spectrum techniques, and anti-jamming protocols for secure military communication.
RATIONALE: Secure communication protects mission integrity and prevents hostile interference.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-019-MILUAV
TITLE: Video Processing
STATEMENT: The video processing component shall implement H.264/H.265 encoding, adaptive bitrate control, and real-time video streaming with automatic quality adjustment and encryption.
RATIONALE: Video processing enables real-time situational awareness for military operations.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-020-MILUAV
TITLE: Network Management
STATEMENT: The network management component shall implement mesh networking, automatic routing, load balancing, and failover mechanisms for robust communication in dynamic environments.
RATIONALE: Network management ensures reliable communication under varying conditions.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4.6 Security Component
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-021-MILUAV
TITLE: Authentication System
STATEMENT: The authentication system shall implement multi-factor authentication, role-based access control, secure session management, and automatic timeout mechanisms for military security requirements.
RATIONALE: Authentication system ensures secure access control and system protection.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-022-MILUAV
TITLE: Threat Detection
STATEMENT: The threat detection component shall implement intrusion detection, anomaly detection, and automatic response mechanisms for cyber and electronic warfare threats.
RATIONALE: Threat detection enables proactive defense against hostile activities.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-023-MILUAV
TITLE: Data Protection
STATEMENT: The data protection component shall implement encryption, secure key management, data integrity checking, and secure data erasure for sensitive military information.
RATIONALE: Data protection ensures confidentiality and integrity of mission data.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4.7 Power Management Component
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-024-MILUAV
TITLE: Battery Management
STATEMENT: The battery management component shall implement real-time monitoring, state-of-charge estimation, thermal management, and automatic low-battery protection for safe operation.
RATIONALE: Battery management ensures safe and efficient power utilization.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-025-MILUAV
TITLE: Power Distribution
STATEMENT: The power distribution component shall implement load balancing, fault detection, automatic load shedding, and redundant power paths for reliable system operation.
RATIONALE: Power distribution ensures reliable power delivery under all conditions.
[[/SECTION]]
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 5. CSCI detailed design
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 5.1 Flight Control Detailed Design
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-026-MILUAV
TITLE: PID Controller Design
STATEMENT: The PID controller shall implement proportional, integral, and derivative control with anti-windup, gain scheduling, and adaptive tuning for optimal flight performance across operating conditions.
RATIONALE: PID controller design ensures stable and responsive flight control.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-027-MILUAV
TITLE: Attitude Estimation
STATEMENT: The attitude estimation shall implement quaternion-based algorithms with gyroscope, accelerometer, and magnetometer fusion using complementary and Kalman filtering techniques.
RATIONALE: Attitude estimation provides accurate orientation information for flight control.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-028-MILUAV
TITLE: Motor Control
STATEMENT: The motor control shall implement PWM-based speed control with current limiting, temperature monitoring, and fault detection for safe and efficient propulsion.
RATIONALE: Motor control ensures reliable propulsion and system safety.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 5.2 Mission Management Detailed Design
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-029-MILUAV
TITLE: Route Planning
STATEMENT: The route planning shall implement A* algorithm with 3D path optimization, obstacle avoidance, fuel efficiency, and mission constraints for optimal mission execution.
RATIONALE: Route planning ensures efficient and safe mission execution.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-030-MILUAV
TITLE: Decision Making
STATEMENT: The decision making shall implement rule-based and machine learning algorithms for autonomous decision-making with safety constraints and human oversight capabilities.
RATIONALE: Decision making enables autonomous operation with safety guarantees.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 5.3 Sensor Fusion Detailed Design
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-031-MILUAV
TITLE: Kalman Filter Design
STATEMENT: The Kalman filter shall implement state estimation for position, velocity, and attitude with process and measurement noise modeling for optimal sensor fusion.
RATIONALE: Kalman filter design provides optimal state estimation from multiple sensors.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-032-MILUAV
TITLE: Point Cloud Processing
STATEMENT: The point cloud processing shall implement LIDAR data filtering, clustering, and obstacle detection algorithms with real-time performance for collision avoidance.
RATIONALE: Point cloud processing enables accurate obstacle detection and avoidance.
[[/SECTION]]
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 6. CSCI data design
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-033-MILUAV
TITLE: Data Structure Design
STATEMENT: The system shall implement efficient data structures for sensor data, mission parameters, flight logs, and communication messages with appropriate memory management and data integrity.
RATIONALE: Data structure design ensures efficient system operation and data reliability.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-034-MILUAV
TITLE: Database Design
STATEMENT: The system shall implement embedded database for mission data, configuration parameters, and system logs with automatic backup, encryption, and data retention policies.
RATIONALE: Database design ensures data persistence and operational accountability.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 7. CSCI interface design
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-035-MILUAV
TITLE: Internal Interface Design
STATEMENT: The system shall implement well-defined internal interfaces between components using message passing, shared memory, and event-driven communication with proper synchronization and error handling.
RATIONALE: Internal interface design ensures reliable component communication and system integration.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-036-MILUAV
TITLE: External Interface Design
STATEMENT: The system shall implement standardized external interfaces for sensors, actuators, communication systems, and ground control stations with protocol compliance and security measures.
RATIONALE: External interface design ensures system interoperability and security.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 8. CSCI resource usage
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-037-MILUAV
TITLE: Memory Usage
STATEMENT: The system shall operate within 512MB RAM and 2GB flash storage with efficient memory management, garbage collection, and memory leak prevention for reliable long-term operation.
RATIONALE: Memory usage constraints ensure system reliability and predictable performance.
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-038-MILUAV
TITLE: Processing Requirements
STATEMENT: The system shall utilize less than 80% of dual-core ARM Cortex-R5 processor capacity under maximum load with proper task scheduling and load balancing.
RATIONALE: Processing requirements ensure system responsiveness and real-time performance.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 9. CSCI requirements traceability
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-039-MILUAV
TITLE: Design Traceability
STATEMENT: All design elements shall be traceable to software requirements with bidirectional traceability maintained throughout the design process for complete verification and validation.
RATIONALE: Design traceability ensures complete requirements implementation and verification.
[[/SECTION]]
[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 10. Notes
[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SDD-040-MILUAV
TITLE: Design Documentation
STATEMENT: All design decisions, architectural choices, and implementation details shall be documented with rationale, alternatives considered, and impact analysis for future maintenance and evolution.
RATIONALE: Design documentation ensures maintainability and knowledge transfer.
[[/SECTION]]
[[/SECTION]]
